    "result": "I fixed it in `hits.go`, but I could not run the tests because the tool needs permission for `go test`.\n\n**Cause:** `Hit` read the whole count, added 1 and wrote the file back. When two processes did this at the same time, both read the same number, so one of the hits was lost.\n\n**Fix:** processes no longer write a shared file.\n- Each process now adds one byte per hit to its own file, `\u003cdir\u003e/\u003cpage\u003e.hits/\u003cpid\u003e`. Only one process writes each file, and no hit reads a value before it writes.\n- `Total` adds up the sizes of those files. It also adds the old `\u003cpage\u003e.count` value, so hits recorded before this change are kept.\n- Each hit makes a file grow by 1 byte, so 1M views use about 1 MB.\n\nI also added `hits_test.go`. It starts 8 separate processes with 4 goroutines each, starting from an old count of 7, and checks that `Total` returns exactly the right number.\n\nTo run it: `go test -count=3 ./...`\n\n**TLDR**\nTwo processes updating the same count file at the same time lost hits. Each process now writes its own file and `Total` adds them up, keeping old counts. The tests are not run yet: `go test -count=3 ./...`",
